{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. You’re here because of worsening abdominal pain and nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started with my usual back pain, then it moved to my stomach. I couldn’t keep anything down, not even my blood pressure pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And this happens about once a month, you said in the ER?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, the back pain flares up, then my stomach just shuts down. It’s like a cycle. I get anxious, then the nausea gets worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Your history of gastroparesis and anxiety probably plays into this. We’ll focus on controlling the pain and nausea so you can eat again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I was in so much pain earlier, but the medicine in the ER helped a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Your vitals are stable now. We’re starting IV fluids because you’ve been dehydrated from not eating. We’ll also keep an eye on your blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My sugar was low in the ER, right? They gave me D50."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was 70, which is low. But it’s stable now. No signs of ketoacidosis, which is good. We’ll continue your regular insulin regimen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ve been trying to stick to my 70/30 insulin. My A1c was 9.3 last time, so I know I need to do better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s actually an improvement. We’ll keep supporting you with your diabetic diet and sliding scale insulin as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my blood pressure? I haven’t taken my lisinopril in days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were hypertensive when you came in—144 over 105. We gave you one dose of lisinopril, and it helped. But we’re watching your kidney function closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My kidneys again? I’ve had issues before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your creatinine was 2.0 when you arrived, which is high for you. It’s come down a bit to 1.8, but not as much as we’d like."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from not drinking enough? Or is my diabetes getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely a mix—dehydration from poor intake, but also possible progression of diabetic nephropathy. We’ve stopped lisinopril for now because it can affect kidneys when they’re stressed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So what will I take instead?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting amlodipine, a different blood pressure medicine that’s safer for your kidneys right now. You’ll take it daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’ll need to follow up with my doctor about this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ve already contacted your PCP to set up urgent follow-up with nephrology. They’ll check your kidney function and adjust meds if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I worry about my kidneys a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. We’re being proactive. Now, about your abdominal pain—your KUB scan showed no blockage or free air, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not appendicitis or something like that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. There’s an air-fluid level in your stomach, which fits with gastroparesis—your stomach isn’t emptying well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s what usually happens. Can I try eating something now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You tolerated clear liquids in the ER, so we’ll start with a light meal. We’ll go slow—small portions, easy to digest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m really hungry. I haven’t eaten in two days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. We’ll get you something soon. We’re also giving ondansetron and ativan for nausea, and continuing your omeprazole for reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been using ativan for anxiety and nausea. It helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ll keep your usual lorazepam doses. We’re also continuing risperidone for your mood, as you’ve been seeing your psychiatrist regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, Dr. ___ has been helping me a lot. The psychotic features have been better lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll keep supporting your mental health. Your ECG showed sinus tachycardia—fast heart rate—but that’s likely from pain, anxiety, and being a bit dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My heart’s been racing. I thought it was anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2127-02-19 15:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a mix. But your heart rate is coming down with fluids and symptom control. No need for extra meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You slept well, I hear. How’s your stomach today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I ate toast and applesauce last night and didn’t feel sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent progress. We’ll advance your diet to regular food today. Still some nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just a little, but not bad. I used the PRN ativan last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’re minimizing narcotics to avoid constipation. You’re walking, blood pressure is better—102 over 50 now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s low, isn’t it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s on the lower side, but you’re not dizzy or weak. Amlodipine can lower it, so we’ll monitor. Your heart rate is 107—still a bit high, but improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel calmer today. Less anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s helping your body recover. We’ll plan for discharge tomorrow if you keep doing this well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2127-02-20 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’d be great. I just want to get back to my routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2127-02-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re officially discharged today. You’ve been eating full meals, pain is controlled, and labs are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2127-02-21 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news. What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2127-02-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your usual meds except lisinopril—we’ve replaced it with amlodipine. Take it daily for blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2127-02-21 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow up with my PCP about my kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2127-02-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and they’ll refer you to nephrology. Also keep seeing your psychiatrist and monitor your blood sugar closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2127-02-21 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for helping me through this flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2127-02-21 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if the pain or nausea comes back, or if you can’t keep fluids down. Otherwise, take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2127-02-19 15:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2127-02-21 12:47:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes and chronic gastroparesis was admitted for worsening abdominal pain and nausea, consistent with a gastroparesis flare triggered by back pain and anxiety. She presented with severe pain and dehydration, requiring IV fluids and pain control. Her symptoms improved with treatment, and she was able to tolerate a full diet by discharge. Labs showed elevated creatinine at 2.0, which decreased to 1.8 but remained concerning for possible progression of diabetic nephropathy. Lisinopril was discontinued due to kidney concerns, and amlodipine was started for blood pressure management. Sinus tachycardia, likely due to pain and anxiety, improved with symptom control. She was discharged home with plans for nephrology follow-up and continuation of her diabetes and psychiatric medications.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Other specified cardiac dysrhythmias",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Backache, unspecified",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Nephritis and nephropathy, not specified as acute or chronic, in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
